# pnpm, matching frontend/. `create-expo-app` scaffolds with npm and that default was never
# a decision; the package-lock.json it produced was removed in favour of one package manager
# across the repo.
#
# node-linker=hoisted is load-bearing, not a preference. Metro resolves modules by walking
# real directories, and several native modules resolve their peers by path rather than by
# request. pnpm's default symlinked layout breaks both — and it breaks them at *bundle* time,
# not install time, so the failure reads as a confusing missing-module trace with nothing in
# it naming the package manager. Do not remove this line.
#
# The switch surfaced one latent bug worth knowing about: jest-expo declares
# @react-native/jest-preset as a PEER dependency, which npm had been satisfying implicitly.
# pnpm does not auto-install peers, so it is now an explicit devDependency — it had been met
# by accident. If a future Expo upgrade fails with "The React Native Jest preset ... has moved
# to a separate package", that dependency needs bumping alongside react-native.
#
# Expo changes fast: read the exact versioned docs (https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v57.0.0/)
# rather than general guides before writing code here.
node-linker=hoisted
